WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.480
One opinion, on one line: Brindlecombe's
late bus must keep running.

2
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.350
Drop it into a letter page.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.300
Then onto a speech card, on a lectern.

4
00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.780
Then into a newspaper
column, and a leaflet panel.

5
00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.320
Every frame stays empty around it.

6
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.020
Same opinion, four different forms.

7
00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:22.160
So what has to change to
make it work in each one?

8
00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.660
In this mission, you'll read
every task for three things:

9
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.920
its form, its audience and its purpose.

10
00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.940
Does the opinion itself have
to change for a new reader?

11
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.280
Or only the first and last lines?

12
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:38.870
And you'll sort sentences by form, and
pick the strongest opening for a speech

13
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.370
about a late bus.

14
00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.420
Your mission: work out what has to change.
